QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Breakfast & Brunch, Cajun/Creole, Cocktail Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":6},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Cocktail Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"W4ZEKkva9HpAdZG88juwyQ","review_id":"LQyC0TRCXTN5kLvyDlW8Ug","date":"2012-01-03T05:11:01","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9497556686401367,"text_excerpt":"Mr. B's was hands down one of the favorite meals of my trip. Great location on the corner of Royal and Iberville and directly across from the Hotel Monteleone. Seeing that it was new years weekend and we hadn't made a reservation, we were told that there would be a 60-70 minute wait. The bar was PACKED and we wouldn't have been able to sit down and enjoy a drink while we waited so we walked across the street and got a round at the Carousel Bar. We returned 45 minutes later and were told that they had already called for our table and that the restaurant was closing so they would \"see what they could do.\" Ending up sitting at the bar which was actually a good thing because we didn't feel ob..."},{"business_id":"W4ZEKkva9HpAdZG88juwyQ","review_id":"GOQDipMS5KMDOvTYBztX2Q","date":"2011-03-16T14:37:16","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9479952454566956,"text_excerpt":"I decided to splurge on Mr. B's! I went for lunch (because they had $1.50 Bloody Marys) and had the BBQ Shrimp, which everyone said was the best BBQ Shrimp in the French Quarter. It was to die for. Decadent sauce over giant shrimp with crusty bread to lap the sauce up with at the end. The waiters came out and bibbed us before it arrived, which was good because we dove right into our plates. This was worth the splurge. One of the best meals in New Orleans!"},{"business_id":"W4ZEKkva9HpAdZG88juwyQ","review_id":"456fsllCJfe0RvP8JCieig","date":"2017-07-23T21:12:11","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9476655721664429,"text_excerpt":"After tasting the BBQ shrimp from Mr. B's last year, I knew I was going to find my way back here whenever I'm in the city. The restaurant is classy and the waiters are dressed to match the atmosphere . Crisp white shirts, bow ties and vests. I've never dined in the dining room, but the bar area is great. There's usually a great mix of customers at the bar and the bartenders are informative and all around awesome. Saturday night was busy, but I found a seat at the bar with no problem. For a starter I ordered the creole gumbo. It was very rich and had a good amount of shrimp, crabmeat and oysters. Not the best gumbo I've had, but it's pretty good. The star of the show for me were the BBQ sh..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"W4ZEKkva9HpAdZG88juwyQ","photo_id":"pSg9G13jBnB1slnQ4_MkhA","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/pSg9G13jBnB1slnQ4_MkhA.jpg","visual_representati